<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Republic - Details of 1997 revenue/expenditure.</title>
<headline>Czech Republic - Details of 1997 revenue/expenditure.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a breakdown of revenue and expenditure of the 1997 Czech state budget approved last week, according to the Finance Ministry: - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>		   CZECH STATE BUDGET REVENUE/EXPENDITURE</p>
<p>						 1996	 1997    pct chg</p>
<p>					     (revised)  (approved)  yr/yr</p>
<p>TOTAL REVENUE				491.0	 549.1   +11.8</p>
<p>TAX REVENUE TOTAL (CZK BLN)	    286.4	 318.6   +11.2</p>
<p>OF WHICH:</p>
<p> Value Added Tax (VAT)		   111.2	 127.8   +14.9</p>
<p> consumption taxes			  61.5	  65.4   + 6.3</p>
<p> individual income tax		    47.9	  55.0   +14.8</p>
<p> corporate income tax (category 1)    10.6	  12.1   +14.2</p>
<p> corporate income tax (category 2)    20.3	  23.8   +17.2</p>
<p> customs tarrifs			    20.3	  19.6   - 3.4</p>
<p> highway taxes   e			   4.3	   4.2   - 2.3</p>
<p> property tax				  4.3	   4.5   + 4.7</p>
<p> motorway users fee			  0.9	   0.9	0</p>
<p> other taxes and fees			5.1	   5.3   + 3.9</p>
<p>SOCIAL INSURANCE PAYMENTS		179.9	 205.5   +14.3</p>
<p>NON-TAX REVENUE TOTAL		     24.7	  25.0   + 1.0</p>
<p>OF WHICH</p>
<p>   capital				     5.8	   4.3   -25.6</p>
<p>   interest payments			 3.4	   3.0   -11.7</p>
<p>   revenue from government credit	7.7	   8.9   +15.8</p>
<p>   other revenue			     7.8	   8.7   +11.9</p>
<p>TOTAL EXPENDITURE			  491.0	 549.1   +11.8</p>
<p>CURRENT EXPENDITURE			428.5	 480.1   +12.0</p>
<p>non-investment subsidies</p>
<p>  to business subjects		    28.0	  29.0    +3.7</p>
<p>  transfers to residents		 184.8	 212.5   +15.0</p>
<p>    of which: pension payments	 130.6	 150.5   +15.2</p>
<p>  state-sector consumption	     182.4	 202.9   +11.2</p>
<p>   debt service			     14.2	  14.4   + 1.9</p>
<p>   foreign transfers			 1.0	   1.5   +50.0</p>
<p>non-investment subsidies</p>
<p>   to local budgets			 18.1	  19.7    +8.8</p>
<p> CAPITAL EXPENDITURE			58.4	  65.3   +11.9</p>
<p>OF WHICH</p>
<p>  invesment subsidies to businesses    5.3	   5.8    +9.4</p>
<p>  public sector investment		45.9	  50.2    +9.3</p>
<p>  investment subsidies to local budgets7.2	   9.3   +30.3</p>
<p> GOVERNMENT PAYMENTS ON CREDIT	   4.1	   3.7   - 9.1</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
